# Secrets. .env.example is the tracked template and stays; a real .env never
# does. Vite's own convention only covers *.local, which left plain .env — the
# exact filename .env.example tells you to create — one `git add .` from being
# committed with the Supabase and PostHog keys in it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
